<title>USA: US Stockpile attracts 8 bidders in aluminum offer.</title>
<headline>US Stockpile attracts 8 bidders in aluminum offer.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-04-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Defense National Stockpile Center said eight companies offered to buy surplus aluminum, including domestic producers.</p>
<p>The bidders were Glencore International, Northwest Aluminum Co, Warlock Wrecking, F&amp;S International, Alcoa, Allied Deals, Metal Exchange Corp, and Sumitomo Corp of America.</p>
<p>The bids totaled 26,533 short tons for $28,304,947. The outcome of the bidding process was due shortly.</p>
<p>((New York Commodity Desk 212-859-1646))</p>
